    "rich_text_UpJPxd": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "text_gyT8nb": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Segment I, featuring our Orb Shell Jacket in Pearled Bone & Denim 410 Bermuda Jeans in Bone Dust:<br/><br/>This shoot wasn’t actually planned. It wasn’t part of the original idea or mood board. But the wind showed up, and we followed where it took us.<br/><br/>As soon as we saw the three moving in synergy, we picked up the camera and captured everything organically, in the moment. Not brothers by blood, but connected through energy and rhythm, they moved with the wind, not against it. The shoot ended up capturing the Orb Shell Jacket in its true form, showing both its beauty and purpose. Made as a traditional windbreaker, the jacket was designed in a clean, minimal way, still windproof, still water-resistant. This moment gave us a rare chance to show the piece not just artistically, but functionally too.<br/><br/>We were honestly stunned at how it all came together. A lot of our strongest shoots seem to happen this way; unplanned, but perfectly aligned.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
